@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Variant - the same flow shown as an interaction overview (nodes = sequence-diagram refs) vs a plain activity (nodes = actions).
'   usecase:      Note the ref-to-interaction distinction that separates interaction-overview from ordinary activity diagrams.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       Diagram-family comparison
' ============================================================================
title Example Interaction Overview (Variant) - Overview vs Activity

' INTERACTION OVERVIEW: nodes are `ref` rectangles pointing at WHOLE interactions.
'   Each node is itself a sequence diagram; zoom in on a node and you see messages.
' PLAIN ACTIVITY: nodes are atomic actions; there is nothing to zoom into.

' Here we render the same order flow with interaction-use nodes.
start
ref over "ReceiveOrder"
fork
  ref over "ChargePayment"
fork again
  ref over "ReserveStock"
end fork
ref over "ShipOrder"
stop

note
  Contrast: a plain activity diagram of this flow would replace each `ref`
  with discrete actions like :receive; :charge; :reserve; :ship;
  The overview version preserves each interaction as a reusable, navigable unit.
end note

@enduml
